---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Opener from '../components/site/Opener.astro';
import Section from '../components/site/Section.astro';
import Ledger from '../components/site/Ledger.astro';

const sources = [
  { label: 'Public filings', body: 'SEC filings and XBRL financial data, for company financials and for benchmarks across sectors.' },
  { label: 'Government statistics', body: 'FRED, the Census Bureau and the Bureau of Labor Statistics, for prices, employment, output and trade.' },
  { label: 'Trade and patent data', body: 'Import and export records and patent filings, for supply chains and for technology positions.' },
  { label: 'Regulatory dockets', body: 'Filings with regulators, for pricing, capacity and market structure in regulated sectors.' },
];
---
<Base
  title="Method · Eleven One Research"
  description="How the work is produced: public sources, figures computed from published data, and dated documents that are not edited after publication."
  current="method"
>
  <Opener
    kicker="Eleven One Research"
    title="Method"
    standfirst="How the work is produced, which sources it uses, and what a reader can check for themselves."
  />

  <Section label="Sources" id="sources">
    <Ledger rows={sources} />
    <p>The practice does not use paid data subscriptions, and every source cited in a piece of work is one that the reader can open.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Figures" id="figures">
    <p>Every chart is computed from a dataset, and the dataset is published beside the piece of work in which the chart appears. A reader can download the data and recompute the figure. Where a chart shows a distribution, the method and its parameters are stated on the page.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Documents of record" id="record">
    <p>A published piece of work is dated and is not edited after publication. If a finding is later revised, the revision is published as a dated addendum, and the original stays as it was.</p>
  </Section>
</Base>
